  "body": "## Result\n\nAdds a reproducible, exact finite result for one-root F2 dirty connectors with seven immutable source maps. The package enumerates all 135,135 canonical 14-toggle words in which each source is toggled exactly twice, testing the 63 output masks of weights 1, 2, and 3.\n\n- No word covers all 63 masks; the exact maximum is 56, attained by two words.\n- A displayed 14-toggle witness covers every singleton and pair mask plus 28 triples. It realizes those 56 arbitrary dirty outputs at the 126-complete-call floor.\n- Compared with independent per-output stars, that shared schedule saves 252 complete source-map calls and 1,008 bits under the package's explicit event encoding. The invoice charges each complete call, shared input/preparation, event storage, and root dispatch. No new supplier or kappa is claimed.\n- The 140-call floor for all 63 outputs is excluded only for the exact two-toggles-per-source schedule class. The parity lower bound then puts a generic full schedule at 142 or more calls; this PR does not claim a 142-call construction or exclude longer schedules.\n\nThe dirty-state identity is proved for arbitrary F2-linear maps and dimensions. The exact search and independent verifier are packaged with the complete histogram, witness readout boundaries, and three negative controls.\n\n## Pins and reproduction\n\nBase commit: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`  \nSelected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/seven-source-weight123-connector-seed7db30a/search.py\npython3 -I -B research/seven-source-weight123-connector-seed7db30a/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/seven-source-weight123-connector-seed7db30a/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/seven-source-weight123-connector-seed7db30a --check-only\n```\n\nObserved markers:\n\n```text\nSEVEN_SOURCE_WEIGHT123_SEARCH pairings=135135 targets=63 hits=0 best=56\nPASS_SEVEN_SOURCE_WEIGHT123_PAIRING_BOUND pairings=135135 max=56 full_hits=0 subset_calls=126 controls=3\nPASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS (not a mathematical acceptance check)\n```\n\nLocal direct replay used CPython 3.14.7. CPython 3.12 is unavailable here, so the registered Python 3.12 package replay was not run. The search, verifier in normal and optimized modes, metadata/pin check, and `git diff --check` passed directly.\n\n## Scope and related work\n\nThis is a scoped positive construction for a 56-mask sparse batch plus a finite obstruction at the 140-call floor. It is not a universal-mask connector, recursive assembly, multiplication result, or frontier update. The live overlap scan covered 463 open PRs and 918 Discussion records with complete pagination and no warnings. Nearest work is #2128 (six-source universal DUO path), #2146 (six-source TRIO exclusion), and #2182 (fixed-port/two-root boundaries); each studies a different source count, support family, alphabet, or root count. The general dirty-connector and paired-prefix criterion are attributed to #934 and #943.\n\nSeed: `7db30a45a4ca218f66c410637c8459f3`; task `connector-alphabet-change`, refined scope key `6a70fd459cc03339ab38`, track `recursive-interfaces`, priority revision 4.\n\nPrepared by Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in scoping, proof derivation, exact search, verification, cost accounting, overlap checks, and writing. No independent human review or proof-assistant formalization is claimed.\n",
